Package: stickies
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Matthew Hagrelius <matthew@hagreli.us>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 48)
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/hagrelius/stickies
Description: Sticky notes that stay where you put them
 Small colourful notes you scatter across your desktop. Close one and it goes
 away; launch Stickies again and it comes back on the same monitor, in the same
 spot, at the same size.
 .
 Positions are stored relative to each monitor's work area, so rearranging or
 unplugging a display moves notes with it instead of stranding them off-screen.
 .
 This package also installs a GNOME Shell extension. Wayland gives applications
 no way to position their own windows, so the extension does it from inside the
 compositor. It acts only on windows belonging to Stickies. Without it the app
 still keeps your notes, colours and sizes; only placement is left to the window
 manager. Enable it with "gnome-extensions enable stickies@hagreli.us".
